    "title": "Fireworks spark deadly Honesdale fire - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Connor Coar ,\n6 hours ago\nHONESDALE, WAYNE COUNTY (WBRE/WYOU) — Officials have uncovered the cause of a deadly house fire in Wayne County .\nAuthorities say fireworks were put into a plastic bag, then discarded in a garbage can on the front porch of this home on 7th Street in Honesdale.\nThe place went up in flames early Tuesday morning.\nSanctuary offers farm animal refuge, promotes peace Two people were able to escape, but the coroner says 23-year-old Sheldon Endriss was found dead near a window on the second floor.\nAn autopsy is set for later this week.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to 28/22 News.\n1",
